arch/"}, {"title": "Connect more of your apps to Search", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/"}, {"title": "AI Mode and AI Overviews updates to explore the web", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/updates-ai-mode-overviews-explore-web/"}, {"title": "Personalize the content you see on Search, Discover, and News", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/personalize-search-discover-news/"}, {"title": "Supporting the web with new features and partnerships", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/tools-partnerships-web-ecosystem/"}, {"title": "7 ways to travel smarter this summer, with help from Google", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/summer-travel-tips-google-search-ai/"}, {"title": "A new way to explore the web with AI Mode in Chrome", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-chrome/"}, {"title": "20 things you didn't know you could do with Search", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/20-things-you-didnt-know-you-could-do-search/"}, {"title": "5 new ways to explore the web with generative AI in Search", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/explore-web-generative-ai-search/"}, {"title": "New ways to connect to the web with AI Overviews", "url": "https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/new-ways-to-connect-to-the-web-with-ai-overviews/"}]}, "The exact phrase is a recurring label on Google Search blog posts rather than the title of one article. The post that best matches it is an AI Mode and AI Overviews update, which appeared about four days ago. Its heading uses the phrase, and it covers clearer inline links, source context, and creator profiles. The label also appears on several other Search posts, including the ones on connecting apps, personalizing Discover, and AI Mode in Chrome.\n\n- **Main match (AI Mode and AI Overviews update):** The post announces changes to AI features so people can explore the web more easily. Google is adding more inline links, sections for official websites, and visual news carousels, along with clickable creator profiles. ([blog.google](https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/updates-ai-mode-overviews-explore-web/))\n- **Connected apps:** Users can link services such as Instacart, Canva, or YouTube Music to AI Mode, which is rolling out first in the U.S. ([blog.google](https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/connected-apps/))\n- **Personalization:** A \"Preferred Sources\" button lets readers add a publisher as a preferred source. Discover users can also tell the feed what topics they want more or less of. ([blog.google](https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/personalize-search-discover-news/))\n- **AI Mode in Chrome:** On desktop, clicking a link opens the webpage beside AI Mode, so users can keep their search context. ([blog.google](https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-chrome/))"], "durationSeconds": 5.584768917, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_018RpoLRuewCPA8gbmDRxsy2", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
